It is an independent implementation of inference for MiniMax H3.
This file lists the third-party material the repository contains or follows,
and what mmh3 works with but does not include.


1. Material in this repository

1.1 ComfyKitchen (Apache License, Version 2.0)

The CPU reference of Sol-Attn in `crates/mmh3-core/src/dit/sparse.rs` follows
the Sol-Attn reference implementation in ComfyKitchen (`comfy_kitchen/backends/eager/sol_attn.py`,)
and the CUDA kernels read the INT8 ConvRot weight format of ComfyKitchen's INT8
layout. The Sol-Attn algorithm is described in arXiv:2607.24027.

